	abstract = {This paper is a short account of the construction of a new class of the infinite-dimensional representations of the quantum groups. The examples include finite-dimensional quantum groups \$U\_q({\textbackslash}mathfrak\{g\})\$, Yangian \$Y({\textbackslash}mathfrak\{g\})\$ and affine quantum groups at zero level \$U\_q({\textbackslash}hat\{{\textbackslash}mathfrak\{g\}\})\_\{c=0\}\$ corresponding to an arbitrary finite-dimensional semisimple Lie algebra \${\textbackslash}mathfrak\{g\}\$. At the intermediate step we construct the embedding of the quantum groups into the algebra of the rational functions on the quantum multi-dimensional torus. The explicit parameterization of the quantum groups used in this paper turns out to be closely related to the parameterization of the moduli spaces of the monopoles. As a result the proposed constructions of the representations provide a quantization of the moduli spaces of the monopoles on \${\textbackslash}RR{\textasciicircum}3\$ and \${\textbackslash}RR{\textasciicircum}2{\textbackslash}times S{\textasciicircum}1\$.},
