	url = {http://arxiv.org/abs/2607.06663},
	doi = {10.1007/JHEP09(2026)248},
	abstract = {Five-dimensional \${\textbackslash}mathcal\{N\}=1\$ superconformal field theories admit a rich variety of generalised global symmetries, including higher-form and 2-group symmetries and their 't\${\textasciitilde}\$Hooft anomalies. We show that this data can be extracted directly from the blow-up equations governing the instanton partition functions of such theories on the \$Ω\$-background. The central object is the classical prefactor \${\textbackslash}exp(-V\_n)\$ weighting each magnetic flux on the blown-up geometry: evaluated on a background for the electric 1-form symmetry, the fractional parts of its exponents encode the cubic self-anomaly of the 1-form symmetry and its mixed anomalies with the instanton, flavour, gravitational, and \${\textbackslash}mathrm\{SU\}(2)\_R\$ symmetries. Combined with the faithful continuous global symmetry of the ultraviolet fixed point, determined from the superconformal index, the same data decides whether the theory possesses a 2-group symmetry or a mixed 't\${\textasciitilde}\$Hooft anomaly. We illustrate the method in gauge theories, including \${\textbackslash}mathrm\{SU\}(4)\$ and \${\textbackslash}mathrm\{USp\}(4)\$ with antisymmetric hypermultiplets and \${\textbackslash}mathrm\{Spin\}(7)\$ and \${\textbackslash}mathrm\{Spin\}(8)\$ with vector hypermultiplets, as well as in several families of non-Lagrangian theories. New results include the effective prepotentials of the \$B\_N\$ and \$B\_N{\textasciicircum}\{(1,2,3)\}\$ families, the cubic 1-form anomalies of the rank-two theories \${\textbackslash}mathbb\{P\}{\textasciicircum}2{\textbackslash}cup{\textbackslash}mathbb\{F\}\_3\$ and \${\textbackslash}mathbb\{P\}{\textasciicircum}2{\textbackslash}cup{\textbackslash}mathbb\{F\}\_6\$, and several mixed 1-form--flavour and 1-form--\${\textbackslash}mathrm\{SU\}(2)\_R\$ anomalies.},
