	abstract = {We consider Iwahori-Coulomb branches \${\textbackslash}mathcal\{A\}\_\{G,{\textbackslash}mathbf\{N\},{\textbackslash}mathbf\{V\}\}{\textasciicircum}\{{\textbackslash}mathrm\{Fl\}\}\$, which are the affine flag analogs of the original Coulomb branches \${\textbackslash}mathcal\{A\}\_\{G,{\textbackslash}mathbf\{N\}\}{\textasciicircum}\{{\textbackslash}mathrm\{Gr\}\}\$ defined by Braverman, Finkelberg, and Nakajima. For any conical symplectic resolution \$X\$, we prove that the \${\textbackslash}mathcal\{A\}\_\{G,{\textbackslash}mathbf\{N\},{\textbackslash}mathbf\{V\}\}{\textasciicircum}\{{\textbackslash}mathrm\{Fl\}\}\$-action on the localized equivariant quantum cohomology of \$X\$, induced by shift operators, satisfies a polynomiality property in terms of stable envelopes. We then study the case \$X = T{\textasciicircum}*(G/P)\$, the cotangent bundle of a flag variety, for which the Iwahori-Coulomb branch is isomorphic to the trigonometric double affine Hecke algebra \${\textbackslash}mathcal\{H\}\_\{G,{\textbackslash}hbar,k\}\$. The polynomiality property enables us to compute explicitly the above action in terms of the Demazure-Lusztig elements and stable envelopes. Applications include: (1) Computation of the Iwarhori-Coulomb branch action for \$G/P\$ by taking the confluent limit, recovering Peterson-Lam-Shimozono's theorem. (2) Construction of an explicit Namikawa-Weyl group action on the equivariant quantum cohomology of \$T{\textasciicircum}*(G/P)\$ that preserves the quantum product, extending a result of Li-Su-Xiong. (3) Proof of a conjecture of Braverman-Finkelberg-Nakajima stating that, up to a shift of the dilation parameter, \${\textbackslash}mathcal\{A\}\_\{G,{\textbackslash}mathfrak\{g\}{\textasciicircum}*\}{\textasciicircum}\{{\textbackslash}mathrm\{Gr\}\}\$ is isomorphic to the spherical subalgebra of \${\textbackslash}mathcal\{H\}\_\{G,{\textbackslash}hbar,k\}\$.},
