	shorttitle = {Orientifold and {Integrability}},
	url = {http://arxiv.org/abs/2610.28725},
	doi = {10.48550/arXiv.2610.28725},
	abstract = {We study planar \${\textbackslash}mathcal\{N\}=4\$ super Yang-Mills theory (SYM) on the real projective space \${\textbackslash}mathbb\{RP\}{\textasciicircum}4\$ using integrability, holography and supersymmetric localization, and discuss its relation to orientifolds in string theory. We show that the integrability of \${\textbackslash}mathcal\{N\}=4\$ SYM is preserved when combining the \${\textbackslash}mathbb\{Z\}\_2\$ involution defining \${\textbackslash}mathbb\{RP\}{\textasciicircum}4\$ with the action of the charge conjugation of the SU\$(N)\$ gauge group. We demonstrate this by calculating one-point functions of non-BPS single-trace operators in various subsectors at weak coupling, which can be mapped to overlaps between energy eigenstates and crosscap states in integrable spin chains. The results exhibit a parity selection rule, a hallmark of integrability, and are given in terms of a ratio of determinants. Building on these results, we conjecture a closed formula for general single-trace operators. We further provide evidence that this construction is holographically dual to a probe orientifold O1-plane in \${\textbackslash}text\{AdS\}\_5{\textbackslash}times {\textbackslash}text\{S\}{\textasciicircum}5\$ by constructing the corresponding worldsheet crosscap states in the pp-wave limit. Finally, we use supersymmetric localization to compute one-point functions of half-BPS operators exactly at finite \$g\_\{{\textbackslash}rm YM\}\$ and \$N\$. The computation reduces to two-dimensional Yang-Mills theory on \${\textbackslash}mathbb\{RP\}{\textasciicircum}2\$ twisted by charge conjugation and leads to a matrix integral of a Wishart-Laguerre type. In the planar limit, the exact result interpolates between the weak-coupling gauge-theory result, the strong-coupling supergravity prediction for the orientifold, and the worldsheet crosscap in the pp-wave limit.},
