	abstract = {This paper tackles the long-standing problem of quantizing the rational spin Ruijsenaars--Schneider model originating in the work of Krichever and Zabrodin. We make use of the technique of quantum Hamiltonian reduction to construct a quantized quiver variety \${\textbackslash}mathfrak\{A\}\_\{N,{\textbackslash}ell\}\$ associated to the framed Jordan quiver. This quantized quiver variety is simultaneously the algebra of quantum observables of the rational spin Ruijsenaars--Schneider model of \$N\$ particles with \${\textbackslash}ell\$ spin polarizations. Inside this algebra, we find a loop algebra and Yangian of \${\textbackslash}mathfrak\{gl\}\_{\textbackslash}ell\$ and conjecture that in the limit of infinitely many particles, the algebra \${\textbackslash}mathfrak\{A\}\_\{N,{\textbackslash}ell\}\$ becomes a shifted affine Yangian. We also exhibit a difference equation for eigenstates of the lowest Hamiltonian that reduces to the spinless case when \${\textbackslash}ell=1\$.},
